// Environment: NMH_MUTATE=<selector> runs one mutant, NMH_ONLY=<HV|REF|P8|U>[,...] restricts a run to parts of the
// package, NMH_CACHE=<directory> keeps the capture of every run of an unchanged program on an unchanged design.
// The normal run sets none of them. SPECIFICATION.md 7.3 to 7.6 give the selectors, the results and the private copies of the design.
//
// MUTATION FIXTURE-HV stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=FIXTURE-HV: run HV is run as prog_hv_nofix, which leaves out the store of the constant $BEEF; shipped design: TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL; page-built copy: TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL; other lines that move on the page-built copy: HV-ANCHOR PASS to NOT GRADED
// MUTATION HV-ANCHOR stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=HV-ANCHOR: run HV samples VPOSR instead of VHPOSR (prog_hv_c); bits 7-0 of VPOSR do not count; shipped design: TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL; page-built copy: TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL; no other line moves on the page-built copy
// MUTATION FIXTURE-UR stimulus red NMH_MUTATE=FIXTURE-UR: run UR is run as prog_ur_nofix, which leaves out the store of the constant; shipped design: TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL; page-built copy: TG68K FAIL, fx68k FAIL; other lines that move on the page-built copy: R2-UR PASS to FAIL
